✅ Encapsulation

“Encapsulation is wrapping data and methods together and restricting direct access to the data using access modifiers. It ensures data security and controlled access via methods.”
Abstraction

“Abstraction is hiding implementation details and exposing only essential functionality using interfaces or abstract classes. It helps reduce complexity and improves flexibility.”
Encapsulation → Bank account (balance is private, accessed via methods)
Abstraction → Payment system (user just calls pay(), doesn’t know internal logic)
Encapsulation → data hiding + control
Abstraction → hiding complexity
Encapsulation is about how data is accessed
Abstraction is about what is exposed

